; examples/macro-author.nx — syntax-quote as the macro author's
; tool, without the `defmacro` sugar (see defmacro.nx for that).
;
; Syntax-quote covers vectors as well as lists, so the
; macroexpander can synthesize the full Lisp shape library:
; `let*` bindings (vector), `fn*` params (vector), `loop*`
; bindings (vector), `cond` clauses (list of pairs).
;
; Host macros are built with FormBuilder directly; a user writes
;
;   (defmacro unless [test & body]
;     \`(if ~test nil (do ~@body)))
;
; The expansion below is the same mechanism without the
; (defmacro ...) wrapper:

(let [name (quote my-binding) value 99]
  ; Construct (let* [my-binding 99] my-binding) — a fully
  ; valid nexis form ready to feed back into the compiler.
  `(let* [~name ~value] ~name))

; -> (let* [my-binding 99] my-binding)
